    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Find the size of the smallest angle in a triangle with side lengths 7 cm, 8 cm and 13 cm. Give your answer correct to the nearest degree.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$28^\\circ$; the smallest angle is opposite the 7 cm side.",
      "worked": "The smallest angle $\\theta$ is opposite the shortest side, 7 cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{8^2+13^2-7^2}{2(8)(13)}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{23}{26}\\\\\\theta&\\approx27.7958^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe smallest angle is $28^\\circ$, correct to the nearest degree.",
